   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of patients with of all forms of TB notified (i.e., bacteriologically confirmed + clinically diagnosed); *includes only those with new and relapse TB.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scope and target assumptions: The COVID-19 pandemic affected efforts to find people with active TB and initiate them on appropriate treatment among countries in the region. Investments made in GC7 support interventions to improve TB case finding so that notifications approach the pre-COVID-19 levels. The number of TB cases notified is expected to increase by 22.5% from 1,047 in 2022 to 1,283 by the end of the grant.
The government of Fiji will full support the NTP and provide FL anti-TB drugs for 550 (2024), 560 (2025) and 571 (2026) notified TB patients. The United States CDC will provide FL anti-TB drugs for a total of 50 patients from three countries (RMI, FSM and Palau) for the entire grant duration. The GC7 grant will procure all reagents and consumables but only 47% (538), 50% (600) and 52% (662) of the required FL anti-TB drugs for the period 2024, 2025 and 2026 respectively. 
Population: The data will come from all the 12 PICs supported by the grant. These are Cook Islands (CK), Fiji (FJ), Federal State of Micronesia (FM), Kiribati (KI), Marshal Islands (MH), Nauru (NA), Nuie (NU), Palau (PW), Samoa (WS), Tonga (TO), Tuvalu (TV) and Vanuatu (VU). 
Data source: National TB register</narrative>
    </description>
