   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of men who have sex with men reached with HIV prevention programs - defined package of services</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scope: This indicator measures the extent of coverage of HIV prevention services for MSM relative to the PSEs. The MSM are expected to be reached with this package of services at least once every 6 months. 
The defined package of services includes the components listed below; 
- HIV prevention communication, information or demand creation for services which should include provider-initiated HIV pre-test counselling
- Provision of consumables (condoms and lubricants)
- Referral to HIV testing and/or STI screening
When data are collected and reported for the number of MSM reached, these individuals should be counted only when they received all components from the above defined package of services. To minimize double counting, countries will use a Unique Identification Code (UIC) to uniquely identify each individual reached. 
100% of the target for period 2024 - 2026 are funded by the Global Fund GC7 grant.
Population: The data will come from all the 12 PICs supported by the grant. These are Cook Islands (CK), Fiji (FJ), Federal State of Micronesia (FM), Kiribati (KI), Marshal Islands (MH), Nauru (NA), Nuie (NU), Palau (PW), Samoa (WS), Tonga (TO), Tuvalu (TV) and Vanuatu (VU). 
Targets assumptions: The focus of the grant is to increase the proportion of MSM reached with HIV prevention services - defined package of services from the baseline of 17% in 2021 to 24% by the end of the grant. The specific assumptions for each country are provided in the Targets Assumptions tab. 
Numerator: Number of men who have sex with men who have received a defined package of HIV prevention services 
Denominator: Estimated number of men who have sex with men in the 12 PICs
Data Source: HIV/ STI prevention and testing registers.</narrative>
    </description>
