   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of people on ART among all people living with HIV at the end of the reporting period</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scope and target assumptions: The greater majority of PLHIV in the region (97%) are from Fiji with the rest of the 11 PICs only adding 69 patients to the 2022 baseline. However, the HIV program in Fiji has had several challenges which have affected their progress on finding and initiating PLHIV on ART. In GC7 the grant will recommence support for key interventions to address these gaps. However, a very conservative 3% increment annually is expected on ART throughout the grant. 
Population: The data will come from all the 12 PICs supported by the grant. These are Cook Islands (CK), Fiji (FJ), Federal State of Micronesia (FM), Kiribati (KI), Marshal Islands (MH), Nauru (NA), Niue (NU), Palau (PW), Samoa (WS), Tonga (TO), Tuvalu (TV) and Vanuatu (VU). 
The projected estimated number of PLHIV for period 2024 - 2026 are from the final 2023 Fiji Spectrum estimates and estimated new cases for the rest of the 11 PICs (additional 2 new cases per year).  
Fiji is expected to meet 100% ART needs for its PLHIV on treatment using government funding and the GC7 grant will cover the remaining 11 PICs. 
Numerator: Number of people on ART at the end of the reporting period 
Denominator: Estimated number of people living with HIV
Data Source: HIV/ STI prevention and testing registers.</narrative>
    </description>
