   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of people in contact with TB patients who began preventive therapy</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scope and target assumptions: Provision of TPT to contacts of bacteriologically confirmed pulmonary TB cases will be prioritized in GC7. Inventions include updating of national guidelines and training of HCWs. CHWs will be provided with transportation costs so that they can visit the communities. The provision of shorter TPT regimens (2HP and 1HP) will make it feasible to put more people on TPT that in the past. It reflects the WHO policy recommendations, the WHO regional TB framework and country specifc workplans to end TB in the Pacific. The assumption calculation was based on: 30% of all contacts will start TPT (number of contacts per index patient Y1-5, Y2- 7, Y3-10). 
Population: The data will come from all the 12 PICs supported by the grant. These are Cook Islands (CK), Fiji (FJ), Federal State of Micronesia (FM), Kiribati (KI), Marshal Islands (MH), Nauru (NA), Nuie (NU), Palau (PW), Samoa (WS), Tonga (TO), Tuvalu (TV) and Vanuatu (VU). 
Data Source: National Latent TB register</narrative>
    </description>
